          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which Snow Joe snow blower is the best?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most buyers with an outdoor outlet nearby, the SJ627E 22-inch corded thrower is the best value, because it never runs out of power and costs far less than a battery machine. For walkways and steps without an outlet, the iON18SB 18-inch cordless model is the better choice, ideally as a second tool."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a Snow Joe handle wet, heavy snow?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only in limited amounts. Single-stage machines with rubber-edged augers move light and moderate snow well but bog down in heavy, wet snow, especially when it is deep. Slow down, take narrower bites and clear before the snow compacts. If heavy snow is normal where you live, a two-stage machine is the better buy."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use a Snow Joe on a gravel driveway?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Every Snow Joe thrower and shovel is single-stage, which means the auger touches the surface to pick up snow. On gravel it throws stones, which is dangerous and damages the auger. Gravel driveways need a two-stage machine with adjustable skid shoes that keep the auger housing above the stones."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do Snow Joe batteries work with other brands?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Snow Joe batteries work with Snow Joe and Sun Joe tools on the same battery platform, but not with EGO, Toro, Greenworks, DeWalt or other tool brands. If you already own batteries from another brand, compare the total cost of a snow tool on that platform before starting a new one."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a Snow Joe cordless snow blower run?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the battery's amp-hour rating, the snow and the temperature. Small cordless throwers have short runtimes that suit walkways and small drives rather than full driveways, and cold weather shortens runtime further. Check the battery included with the specific model and keep it warm indoors until you use it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a Snow Joe electric shovel worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If you clear steps, decks, balconies or narrow paths regularly, yes. A power shovel turns a tiring job into a quick one and suits people who should not lift heavy snow. It is not a driveway tool. Its narrow path and short throw make large surfaces slow, so pair it with a bigger machine if you have a driveway."
          }
