        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Snow Joe is the right brand when the job is small and the budget is tight. The SJ627E corded thrower is the best value in the lineup for a short paved driveway near an outlet, the iON18SB is a well-judged cordless machine for walkways and steps, and the electric shovels are the easiest way to keep steps and decks clear.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Where Snow Joe falls short is size, depth and surface: long driveways, heavy wet snow, plow ridges and gravel. If those describe your winter, buy a bigger machine for the driveway and keep a Snow Joe for everything around it.
          </p>
